(2503165, 343524, 29293, '<td valign="top">i think the heavy borader takes away, i find this difficult as maybe you got a comment before to make the border more</td>', 'i think the heavy borader takes away, i find this difficult as maybe you got a comment before to make the border more', '2006-06-09 20:49:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(2503178, 342740, 42125, '<td valign="top">It wasn''t able to find the original until you posted in the forum.<br/>Yes you have improved it a bit but there are still things that could be better.<br/>I like the colours better on your previous but this one is better lit.<br/>I like the background better on your previos if you skip the clothing in front.<br/>The wooden thing under is ok, but the walls are distracting because of they are made of three different colours and textures. One thing is for sure, you have made it much lighter and in good focus. Bumping up a bit cause I found your original and could make the comparison :-)</td>', 'It wasn''t able to find the original until you posted in the forum.Yes you have improved it a bit but there are still things that could be better.I like the colours better on your previous but this one is better lit.I like the background better on your previos if you skip the clothing in front.The wooden thing under is ok, but the walls are distracting because of they are made of three different colours and textures. One thing is for sure, you have made it much lighter and in good focus. Bumping up a bit cause I found your original and could make the comparison :-)', '2006-06-09 20:53:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(2503241, 342990, 29293, '<td valign="top">i hate cat photos but the contrast on this is purrfect</td>', 'i hate cat photos but the contrast on this is purrfect', '2006-06-09 21:10:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(2503460, 342687, 53147, '<td valign="top">Well unless there are a couple of people walking down this path and taking pics I may guess who I am commenting on. This is very nice and I will probably bump it up come end of week. Great detail, great colors, great lines. This has the feel that I was wishing the first one had. And the peek up into the sky outside the corridor is a nice little treat to top the whole shot off. This should easily do better than the original. Beautiful shot Deb.<br/> <br/>Edit: So there are two of you in the same place. So now I edit my critique for you Sandy. Everything stands the same including the feel you have on this one compared to your original. The detail and postprocessing stand out way better in this one. A great feel, presentation and fantsastic detail to this shot and I would expect it to do better in score over your original - even though you had a pretty good score to start with. I will still most likely come back later on and give this a bump - so expect another edit.<br/> <br/>Edit - Bet this is the longest comment post you have ever gotten during a challenge before huh? Bumping up (but dont tell Melethia)</td>', 'Well unless there are a couple of people walking down this path and taking pics I may guess who I am commenting on. This is very nice and I will probably bump it up come end of week. Great detail, great colors, great lines. This has the feel that I was wishing the first one had. And the peek up into the sky outside the corridor is a nice little treat to top the whole shot off. This should easily do better than the original. Beautiful shot Deb. Edit: So there are two of you in the same place. So now I edit my critique for you Sandy. Everything stands the same including the feel you have on this one compared to your original. The detail and postprocessing stand out way better in this one. A great feel, presentation and fantsastic detail to this shot and I would expect it to do better in score over your original - even though you had a pretty good score to start with. I will still most likely come back later on and give this a bump - so expect another edit. Edit - Bet this is the longest comment post you have ever gotten during a challenge before huh? Bumping up (but dont tell Melethia)', '2006-06-09 22:59:14.000000', NULL, 1),
