(2524145, 343526, 51802, '<td valign="top"><b>Hello from the Critique Club!</b> <br/> <br/>My first impression is very positive.  I don''t usually like high key photos, but this one is very well done.  A lot of people seem to over expose their photos and call it high key.  I am glad you did not do this.  <br/> <br/>Your pose adds to the interest.  You obeyed the rule of thirds, your attention is not on the camera, and your head is tilted to one side.  These elements make this a more dynamic shot and give the viewer the impression that more is happening that you just having your photo taken.<br/> <br/>Overall this is a very nice self portrait!<br/> <br/>-Bill</td>', 'Hello from the Critique Club!  My first impression is very positive.  I don''t usually like high key photos, but this one is very well done.  A lot of people seem to over expose their photos and call it high key.  I am glad you did not do this.   Your pose adds to the interest.  You obeyed the rule of thirds, your attention is not on the camera, and your head is tilted to one side.  These elements make this a more dynamic shot and give the viewer the impression that more is happening that you just having your photo taken. Overall this is a very nice self portrait! -Bill', '2006-06-17 11:57:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(2524400, 343224, 14414, '<td valign="top">Wow, congrats on the PB and 7+ with this great shot.<br/> <br/>Slightly different format for Take Two...<br/> <br/><i><b>Main critiques on original</b></i> <br/>brightness on right, more water reflection/detail, noisy sky, distracting bits (to be cropped out but you''ve just made them non-distracting)<br/> <br/><i><b>What you''ve improved</b></i> <br/>Much better POV, without the teenagers to get in the way. Reflection really adds to it, and colours are more vibrant, without such noise.Because you''ve not had to crop in so tightly its compositionally much stronger. Also, maybe its just rfom the wider angle, but you''ve managed to avoid blowing out the brightest parts this time. Because the whole ship is in view, you''ve captured more of a sense of its grandeur, so it makes much more of an impact. Also, it avoids the clutteredness of the original.<br/> <br/>Oh, and I much prefer this border, much neater imho.<br/> <br/><i><b>What I prefer about the original</b></i> <br/>Whilst I love the reflection of the 2nd, I have to admit I prefer the position of where boat meets sea in the original - I think I''d like to see this one cropped to just below the porthole reflection<br/> <br/><b><i>Overall, imho</i></b> <br/>Great work, you should be proud of it. Definitely deserved the score/placement, and its nice to see you do so well when I''ve seen the first photo and really can see the improvements.</td>', 'Wow, congrats on the PB and 7+ with this great shot. Slightly different format for Take Two... Main critiques on original brightness on right, more water reflection/detail, noisy sky, distracting bits (to be cropped out but you''ve just made them non-distracting) What you''ve improved Much better POV, without the teenagers to get in the way. Reflection really adds to it, and colours are more vibrant, without such noise.Because you''ve not had to crop in so tightly its compositionally much stronger. Also, maybe its just rfom the wider angle, but you''ve managed to avoid blowing out the brightest parts this time. Because the whole ship is in view, you''ve captured more of a sense of its grandeur, so it makes much more of an impact. Also, it avoids the clutteredness of the original. Oh, and I much prefer this border, much neater imho. What I prefer about the original Whilst I love the reflection of the 2nd, I have to admit I prefer the position of where boat meets sea in the original - I think I''d like to see this one cropped to just below the porthole reflection Overall, imho Great work, you should be proud of it. Definitely deserved the score/placement, and its nice to see you do so well when I''ve seen the first photo and really can see the improvements.', '2006-06-17 15:23:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(2525830, 343224, 37334, '<td valign="top">Hi from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>What a great image! <br/> <br/>This image has an unreal quality to it, it''s almost too perfect:)) Those wonderful glass like reflections are almost as though you slipped a mirror below the boat, as the water is so smooth and flawless.<br/> <br/>The lighting too, gives an unreal feeling; it''s as if you picked up the boat and put it in a studio, so that you could have complete control of the lighting and colour:)) There is a gorgeous balance to the intensity of the lighting - with the brightest light being on the boat in the middle of the image, and then it gradually fades in intensity as you move away from the middle, at both the top and bottom of the composition. The lighting on the upper masts and sails looks as though it has been painted in oils;)<br/> <br/>The whole image creates a feeling of calm and serenity, and as others have said, it''s practically flawless, so there is little more I can add;)</td>', 'Hi from the Critique Club! What a great image!  This image has an unreal quality to it, it''s almost too perfect:)) Those wonderful glass like reflections are almost as though you slipped a mirror below the boat, as the water is so smooth and flawless. The lighting too, gives an unreal feeling; it''s as if you picked up the boat and put it in a studio, so that you could have complete control of the lighting and colour:)) There is a gorgeous balance to the intensity of the lighting - with the brightest light being on the boat in the middle of the image, and then it gradually fades in intensity as you move away from the middle, at both the top and bottom of the composition. The lighting on the upper masts and sails looks as though it has been painted in oils;) The whole image creates a feeling of calm and serenity, and as others have said, it''s practically flawless, so there is little more I can add;)', '2006-06-18 08:25:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(2525897, 343224, 60552, '<td valign="top">This is a great image. I could kick myself every time I get an hour away from a shot and realize the conditions are better.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-06-18 09:26:27.</i></td>', 'This is a great image. I could kick myself every time I get an hour away from a shot and realize the conditions are better.', '2006-06-18 10:26:03.000000', '2006-06-18 10:26:27.000000', 0),
(2525968, 343696, 50674, '<td valign="top">Til hamingju með nýtt persónulegt met! Mér finnst þær báðar mjög góðar, sú fyrri var ein af fyrstu myndunum sem ég skoðaði hér a DPC, aha hugsaði ég, hér eru greinilega Íslendingar. Hvort þeir eru :)<br/>Verðskuldaður borði.</td>', 'Til hamingju með nýtt persónulegt met! Mér finnst þær báðar mjög góðar, sú fyrri var ein af fyrstu myndunum sem ég skoðaði hér a DPC, aha hugsaði ég, hér eru greinilega Íslendingar. Hvort þeir eru :)Verðskuldaður borði.', '2006-06-18 11:30:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(2526760, 342723, 43434, '<td valign="top"><b>Hi from the critique club</b> <br/> <br/><b>First impressions</b> <br/>I really like this shot .. but my preference was  the first one ... it left more to the imagination .. and teased the mind a little more.<br/> <br/><b>Subject</b> <br/>This meets the challenge, head on ... and streaming away.<br/> <br/><b>Composition</b> <br/>The composition is good, the use of the bullet on the thirds line in excellent ... the words going up the inside of the vertical thirds is excellent.<br/> <br/><b>Technicals</b> <br/>This is very high key .. and for that it works .. I know you have taken on the comments recieved .. and it shows that your orginal worked extremely well .. and sometimes on executing the changes suggested ... it no longer works as well.  <br/> <br/>The picture has very good focus ... and great motion capture ... there is not as much fluid as the first shot .. and I think this makes a different.<br/> <br/><b>Improving</b> <br/>Stick to the original ... it was great ... it is hard to replicate and get better scores .. unless you are replicating a low scorer in the first place.<br/> <br/><b>Final word</b> <br/>You did great .. took on the comments .. and really made a go of it ... good work .. keep it up.<br/> <br/>If you have any comments on this critique feel free to PM me.<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', 'Hi from the critique club  First impressions I really like this shot .. but my preference was  the first one ... it left more to the imagination .. and teased the mind a little more. Subject This meets the challenge, head on ... and streaming away. Composition The composition is good, the use of the bullet on the thirds line in excellent ... the words going up the inside of the vertical thirds is excellent. Technicals This is very high key .. and for that it works .. I know you have taken on the comments recieved .. and it shows that your orginal worked extremely well .. and sometimes on executing the changes suggested ... it no longer works as well.   The picture has very good focus ... and great motion capture ... there is not as much fluid as the first shot .. and I think this makes a different. Improving Stick to the original ... it was great ... it is hard to replicate and get better scores .. unless you are replicating a low scorer in the first place. Final word You did great .. took on the comments .. and really made a go of it ... good work .. keep it up. If you have any comments on this critique feel free to PM me. Kari', '2006-06-18 20:28:55.000000', NULL, 0),
