(2540895, 343727, 30049, '<td valign="top">Harv - I meant to comment on this before.  The sharpness of this image really jumps out at me.  You forgot to mention in your comments another factor in the difference between this shot and your ''Grace'' shot from 2003...equipment!  ;^)<br/> <br/>Smile and keep having fun!</td>', 'Harv - I meant to comment on this before.  The sharpness of this image really jumps out at me.  You forgot to mention in your comments another factor in the difference between this shot and your ''Grace'' shot from 2003...equipment!  ;^) Smile and keep having fun!', '2006-06-22 12:39:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(2541105, 343059, 28710, '<td valign="top">Nicely improved sky... I''d probably still push that blue a bit and I might have considered doing something with the fronds in the Palm tree... Maybe adding a bit of color... (layer, selective color, eraser)<br/> <br/>Definitely improved though...</td>', 'Nicely improved sky... I''d probably still push that blue a bit and I might have considered doing something with the fronds in the Palm tree... Maybe adding a bit of color... (layer, selective color, eraser) Definitely improved though...', '2006-06-22 13:53:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(2544042, 343830, 41337, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from CTP2</b> <br/> <br/>I think you improved this shot in the wow factor category. It no longer looks like a snapshot compared to the other one. It''s bold and in your face. However, there are some things I prefer in the original. For example, the sharpness. I think you got it right in the original but here it feels oversharpened. Maybe I''m wrong but this type of texture shouldn''t look that sharp, IMO. The other thing is the background color. I liked the black background better than this bright red version, which just makes the image seem too bright in general. Still it commands your attention better than the original so good job improving that.</td>', 'Greetings from CTP2  I think you improved this shot in the wow factor category. It no longer looks like a snapshot compared to the other one. It''s bold and in your face. However, there are some things I prefer in the original. For example, the sharpness. I think you got it right in the original but here it feels oversharpened. Maybe I''m wrong but this type of texture shouldn''t look that sharp, IMO. The other thing is the background color. I liked the black background better than this bright red version, which just makes the image seem too bright in general. Still it commands your attention better than the original so good job improving that.', '2006-06-23 05:07:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(2544054, 343668, 41337, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from CTP2</b> <br/> <br/>Congrats on your personal best. The execution is much cleaner this go around. Also nice touch with that duality of fantasy vs reality conveyed with the background. That really hammered home the idea to voters who couldn''t get it the first time. The only thing I feel held this back from winning was the reflections and flare. I''d probably just use backlighting only for this type of setup.</td>', 'Greetings from CTP2  Congrats on your personal best. The execution is much cleaner this go around. Also nice touch with that duality of fantasy vs reality conveyed with the background. That really hammered home the idea to voters who couldn''t get it the first time. The only thing I feel held this back from winning was the reflections and flare. I''d probably just use backlighting only for this type of setup.', '2006-06-23 05:18:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(2546986, 343689, 40370, '<td valign="top">Just cruisin'' through my favs tonight, looked up the original "baby deer" and found definite enrichment in this image. I didn''t enter or vote on this challenge (although have many to improve on :), I couldn''t imagine voting and trying to look up originals (as only a few might be recognizable anyway) and give credit for images that were truly better. I love your work and this shot definitely shows that you thought about what would make it outstanding.</td>', 'Just cruisin'' through my favs tonight, looked up the original "baby deer" and found definite enrichment in this image. I didn''t enter or vote on this challenge (although have many to improve on :), I couldn''t imagine voting and trying to look up originals (as only a few might be recognizable anyway) and give credit for images that were truly better. I love your work and this shot definitely shows that you thought about what would make it outstanding.', '2006-06-23 22:27:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(2548964, 341578, 30454, '<td valign="top">Greetings from your own critique club. <br/> <br/><b>First Impression</b> <br/>Colors add little more to this comapre to the original. <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>Height is just 393 pixels. I would like to see more height.<br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Improvement over the origianl in terms of colors and interesting coulds. But the composition is almost smae. I don''t know if there were any comments on the original about the height.<br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>The color and lighting okay.<br/><b>Improvement:</b> <br/>Different composition which allows more height.<br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Just notices the take two is almost same score as the original.<br/> <br/>Keep Shooting, Cheers!!!</td>', 'Greetings from your own critique club.  First Impression Colors add little more to this comapre to the original. Composition: Height is just 393 pixels. I would like to see more height.Subject: Improvement over the origianl in terms of colors and interesting coulds. But the composition is almost smae. I don''t know if there were any comments on the original about the height.Technical (Colour and light): The color and lighting okay.Improvement: Different composition which allows more height.Summary: Just notices the take two is almost same score as the original. Keep Shooting, Cheers!!!', '2006-06-24 16:05:44.000000', NULL, 0),
