(2744106, 341976, 15711, '<td valign="top">I loved this during the challenge. Don''t know why I never commented. The composition and colors. Has a sadness about it.  Immediately, what comes to mind is a famous song of the 40''s with the same title.<br/> <br/>A little dream castle<br/>With every dream gone<br/>Is lonely and silent<br/>The shades are all drawn<br/>And my heart is heavy<br/>As I gaze upon <br/>A cottage for sale<br/>The lawn we were proud of<br/>Is waving in hay <br/>A beautiful garden<br/>Has withered away<br/>Where you planted roses <br/>The weeds seem to say<br/>A cottage for sale<br/>From every single window<br/>I see your face<br/>But when I reach the window<br/>There''s empty space <br/>The key''s in the mailbox<br/>The same as before <br/>But no one is waiting <br/>For me anymore<br/>The end of our story<br/>Is there on the door<br/>A cottage for sale<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-08-20 17:55:00.</i></td>', 'I loved this during the challenge. Don''t know why I never commented. The composition and colors. Has a sadness about it.  Immediately, what comes to mind is a famous song of the 40''s with the same title. A little dream castleWith every dream goneIs lonely and silentThe shades are all drawnAnd my heart is heavyAs I gaze upon A cottage for saleThe lawn we were proud ofIs waving in hay A beautiful gardenHas withered awayWhere you planted roses The weeds seem to sayA cottage for saleFrom every single windowI see your faceBut when I reach the windowThere''s empty space The key''s in the mailboxThe same as before But no one is waiting For me anymoreThe end of our storyIs there on the doorA cottage for sale', '2006-08-20 18:54:32.000000', '2006-08-20 18:55:00.000000', 0),
